# Unbound Flourishing's real "whenever you cast a permanent spell with {X}"
# trigger (Mode$ SpellCast | HasXManaCost$ True, TriggerSpellAbilityCastOrCopy
# .java:171-181) fires off Farmer Cotton ({X}{G}{W}, X = 1) and goes on the
# stack above it. ai's Counterspell, cast on top of both, counters Farmer
# Cotton first; the trigger's DB$ ChangeX | Defined$ TriggeredSpellAbility
# then resolves against a spell no longer on the stack, which is a no-op,
# not an error (changexeffect.go): Java writes the new X onto an orphaned
# SpellAbility nothing reads again.
#
# What this pins: Unbound Flourishing's and Farmer Cotton's real scripts run
# through casting, the trigger and ChangeX without an error. What it cannot
# tell apart: whether the trigger fired at all -- the end state is the same
# either way -- so firing is pinned at module level
# (TestSpellCastTriggerHasXManaCost*, xannounced_test.go).
#
# Nor can it show the doubled X itself. expect.state has no stack
# and no X, and every real {X} permanent reads X back only through
# Count$xPaid or etbCounter, neither resolved yet -- so letting Farmer Cotton
# resolve would fail on its own ETB Token, not on ChangeX. The doubling is
# proven at module level instead (TestUnboundFlourishingDoublesX,
# changexvalue_test.go), against the same verbatim trigger lines.
startturn human
advance 3
tapformana human 2 G
tapformana human 3 G
tapformana human 4 W
queue payx 1
queue paygeneric G
castspell human 1
tapformana ai 7 U
tapformana ai 8 U
queue targets 1
castspell ai 9
resolvestack
